Two exceptions, granted deliberately and limited in scope:

1. Security audit. The external auditor receives a frozen commit and may build,
   run and publish findings about it. The audit report itself is published
   after gate G-4.
2. Bug-bounty research. Anyone may run a local copy for the sole purpose of
   finding and responsibly reporting defects under SECURITY.md.

The license of a third-party dependency always governs that dependency. The
economy constants in packages/economy and the docs/ specification are offered
as-is with no warranty; they describe the rules the on-chain programs enforce,
and where the two disagree the deployed program is right.
